  (before and after neoadjuvant therapy, early after surgery and after long-term follow-up) and were included in the    
  present study. RESULTS There were no statistically significant differences in the global GIQLI index between          
  patients treated with neoadjuvant radiochemotherapy with and without hyperthermia at any time point. The              
