70-75 Gy) to the primary site. Twenty-seven patients underwent a second series of measurements early in the course of 
irradiation. RESULTS Sixty-three patients underwent pretreatment tumor oxygen assessment (primary site, n = 24; nodes, n
= 39). The median pO2 for primary lesions was 4.8 mmHg, and it was 4.3 mmHg for cervical nodes. There was a weak 
association between anemia and more poorly oxygened tumors, but many non-anemic patients still had poorly oxygenated 
tumors. Repeat assessments of tumor oxygenation after 10-15 Gy were unchanged compared to pretreatment baselines. Poorly
oxygenated nodes pretreatment were more likely to contain viable residual disease at post-radiation neck dissection. 
